Task 1: Create Smart Inventories with Filters for Host Selection
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Smart Inventories
Smart inventories are dynamic collections of hosts that automatically update based on defined criteria. Unlike static inventories, smart inventories use filters to dynamically include or exclude hosts based on their properties.

Key Benefits:

Dynamic Updates: Automatically adjust as infrastructure changes
Flexible Targeting: Use complex criteria for host selection
Reduced Maintenance: No manual inventory updates required
Scalability: Handle large, changing environments efficiently
