Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Smart Inventory Shows No Hosts
Symptoms: Smart inventory appears empty despite having matching hosts.

Solutions:

# Check filter syntax
# Ensure variables are properly defined on hosts
# Verify case sensitivity in filters
# Test with simpler filters first
Example Fix:

Original filter: Server_Type:Web (incorrect case)
Corrected filter: server_type:web
Issue 2: Job Fails on Smart Inventory
Symptoms: Jobs fail when run against smart inventories but work with static inventories.

Solutions:

Verify all hosts in the smart inventory are accessible
Check that host variables are properly set
Ensure playbook logic handles dynamic host sets
Issue 3: Filter Not Working as Expected
Symptoms: Smart inventory includes unexpected hosts or excludes expected ones.

Debugging Steps:

Test filters incrementally
Use the AWX interface to preview filter results
Check host variable definitions
Verify operator syntax
Advanced Smart Inventory Patterns
Pattern 1: Environment-Based Inventories
# Development environment
environment:development

# Non-production environments
environment:!production

# Multiple environments
environment:development or environment:staging
Pattern 2: Resource-Based Inventories
# High-performance servers
cpu_cores:>=8 and memory_gb:>=16

# Low-resource servers
cpu_cores:<=4 and memory_gb:<=8

# Balanced servers
cpu_cores:>=4 and cpu_cores:<=8 and memory_gb:>=8 and memory_gb:<=16
Pattern 3: Location-Based Inventories
# US regions
region:~us-.*

# East coast regions
region:us-east or region:us-northeast

# Exclude specific regions
region:!us-west
Best Practices for Smart Inventories
1. Naming Conventions
Use descriptive names that indicate the filter criteria
Include the purpose or use case in the name
Maintain consistency across your organization
2. Filter Design
Start with simple filters and add complexity gradually
Test filters thoroughly before using in production
Document complex filter logic for team understanding
3. Host Variable Management
Establish consistent variable naming conventions
Ensure all relevant hosts have required variables
Use meaningful variable values that support filtering
4. Performance Considerations
Avoid overly complex filters that impact performance
Consider the frequency of inventory updates
Monitor job execution times with large smart inventories
